# The encri-api commit Encri Files is built against (F9).
#
# Encri Files builds encri-api's client from source, as an included build beside this checkout
# (settings.gradle.kts, F1), so that source is an input to every APK. A developer's checkout uses whatever
# ../encri-api holds. Every other build puts encri-api at this commit first, through scripts/ci/encri-api:
# ci.yml, reproducible.yml and scripts/release/reproduce.sh. So a release names the encri-api it was built
# from by this line in its tagged tree, which a reproducible build needs (encri D116, D126).
#
# Bump it in the commit that needs the newer encri-api. The pre-push hook refuses a push while ../encri-api
# is anywhere else, because the unit tests it runs would then have tested a different encri-api from the one
# CI builds. Push encri-api first: CI fetches the commit from the repository below.
repository=https://github.com/syshlted/encri-api.git
commit=c27f139dfbc2efab5910a91d053b904019f28321
